<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n98744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύμπλοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμπλήρ-πλους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sailing with</i> one in a ship,
				<i>shipmate</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.41
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ephor.
				27J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.148a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				1207
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.21
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύμπλοι ἢ συστρατιῶται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					556c
				</span></i>
			; poet. of ships, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς ς. εἰς ἄγρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.381
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Etrusc.
			</span></i>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				585
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>partner</i> or <i>comrade in</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάθους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					541
				</span></i>
			.</div>
